  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1258 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nShowers and thunderstorms are possible this afternoon and evening\nas a cold front sweeps through the region. Dry conditions should\nthen follow overnight behind the front. Monday is looking to be\ndry now as the front will be south enough so additional showers\nand thunderstorms should not clip the southern portion of the CWA.\n\nThe next noteworthy chances for rain/storms look to come late \nMonday night into Tuesday as the front lifts back north and a \nshortwave tracks through the western Great Lakes region. Rain \nchances will then continue Tuesday night into Wednesday as \nadditional shortwaves move through the region and the front \nremains close enough to our area to influence our weather.\n\nHigh pressure builds in across the area Wednesday night, pushing\nthe front south and generally keeping the area dry through the\nrest of the work week. The high eventually shifts east, allowing\nfor the chance for showers and thunderstorms to return to the area\nnext weekend.\n\nTemperatures will generally be in the upper 70s to lower 80s\nthrough mid week, decreasing into the 70s for the back portion of\nthe work week into next weekend.",
